    "text": "{\n  \"semantic_type\": \"dimension\",\n  \"unit\": null,\n  \"additive_over_entities\": null,\n  \"additive_over_time\": null,\n  \"time_rollup\": null,\n  \"valid_methods\": [],\n  \"period_basis\": null,\n  \"derivation\": null,\n  \"calendar\": null,\n  \"seasonal_adjustment\": null,\n  \"annualized\": null,\n  \"entity_grain\": null,\n  \"hierarchy\": null,\n  \"comparability\": null,\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"source\": \"SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts API\",\n    \"url_template\": \"https://data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyfacts/CIK{cik}.json\",\n    \"retrieved_on\": \"2026-10-24\"\n  },\n  \"description\": \"Label column for a long-format fundamentals table. It names which financial measure the row's value holds. The 7 values are capex, diluted_eps, net_income, op_cash_flow, operating_income, revenue and total_assets. The measures differ in kind: capex, net_income, op_cash_flow, operating_income and revenue are period flows in USD; diluted_eps is per-share in USD/shares; total_assets is an instant-in-time stock in USD. Values must not be aggregated across different metric labels. Filter to a single metric before aggregating. Each label is mapped from an XBRL concept, and the concept can differ by company. For example, DRI's op_cash_flow uses the continuing-operations variant of the concept. Check the concept column when comparing across tickers.\"\n}",
